": "request_review", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 909460, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01KpoQ8Z6SkRJJFpXgJAtumj", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 916503, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **The bug:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded half-cents up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), even though its docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212). So `2.665` came out as `2.67` instead of the `2.66` the test expects.\n- **The fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I changed it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Now `2.665` rounds to `2.66` and `2.675` still rounds to `2.68`, matching the test.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that commit (`08d3cd5986`).\n- **Pull request:** The request to open the PR timed out, but it had actually gone through, so I didn't open a second one. The PR had no reviewers attached, so I added alex separately.\n\nI couldn't find FIN-212 in the advisory system (\"unknown advisory\"), so I relied on the code's docstring and the test for the intended behaviour. I haven't merged the PR, since that needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01JmQp6x1rZnBQkQK1JSEGHs", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_015kHayC1VgX73jmZ91C3hEE", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01YbMdarZXW7Rt4LXa7mHdgZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use"